    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Welcome to this exceptional 4-bedroom detached residence extending to c. 2,600 sq. ft., set on a mature and beautifully landscaped c. 0.70-acre site enjoying scenic countryside views in a fabulous setting. Approached via electric gates, the cobble-lock driveway is lined with striking plants, trees, and shrubs, as well as an impressive water feature that sets a truly elegant tone on arrival. Upon entering, the sense of space and quality is immediate. The generous accommodation comprises an inviting entrance hallway, impressive living room, snug, a spacious kitchen/dining room, games room & bar, complemented by a utility room, a double bedroom, and a guest WC—all on the ground floor. Upstairs, a bright and airy landing leads to three further double bedrooms . The master suite enjoys the added luxury of an en-suite and walk-in wardrobe. While the interior delivers comfort and sophistication, the external space is equally outstanding. Patio doors open onto a beautifully landscaped enclosed rear garden with sunny aspect, designed with multiple areas perfect for outdoor living and relaxation. A large detached garage sits to the side of the property, ideal for a wide range of uses. This superb home offers the very best of countryside living while remaining easily accessible to all essential amenities. Wexford Town is less than 13km away, providing restaurants, shops, schools, and more. Nearby villages such as Barntown and Glynn/Killurin offer further local facilities. Access to the N25 is just 1km away, with the M11 only 15km—making Dublin Airport a manageable 2-hour drive, and Rosslare Europort just 25 minutes . Many of Wexford’s renowned beaches—including Rosslare, Kilmore Quay, and Carne—are also close by. An ideal family home in a superb location—viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this beautiful property has to offer. Properties of its kind are rare to hit the open market.\r\n\r\nVIEWING IS HIGHLY RECOMMENDED"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Property Accommodation\r\nEntrance Hallway – (5.77m x 5.01m), Part tiled/part carpet flooring, coving\r\nSitting Room – (6.92m x 5.48m), Feature fireplace, wooden flooring, bay window, double doors to diner.\r\nGames Room – (6.74m x 5.48m), Fully fitted & built in bar, feature stone wall, stove, wooden flooring, double door to outside.\r\nFamily Room – (7.00m x 3.17m), Feature fireplace, bay window, wooden flooring, feature ceiling recess, recessed lighting, coving.\r\nKitchen/Dining – (8.76m x 3.65m), Fully fitted eye and waist level units, tiled floors, part tiled walls, Aga cooker, coving, recessed lighting, centre rose, double doors to kitchen/diner.\r\nPlayroom – (4.00m x 3.13m), Carpet flooring, built in storage.\r\nUtility Room – (2.93m x 1.71m), Plumbed for appliances, stainless steel sink unit, eye and waist level units, tiled floor, part tiled walls.\r\nBedroom No. 1 –  (3.09m x 3.15m), Wooden flooring, built in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nLanding – (2.96m x 3.86m)\r\nBedroom No. 2 – (2.50m x 5.42m), Wooden flooring\r\nBathroom – (2.91m x 2.64m), WC, WHB, corner bath, tiled floor, shower.\r\nBedroom No. 3 – (3.15m x 3.71m) Wooden flooring.\r\nMaster Bedroom – (4.85m x 3.65m) Wooden flooring, walk in wardrobe with fitted storage.\r\nEn-Suite – (2.26m x 2.01m), Shower, WHB, WC, Tiled floor.\r\n\r\nOutside: Mature gardens to front and rear, garage.\r\nServices: Electricity, private water, private sewerage, oil fired central heating.\r\nBER: C1 Ber No: 108759184 Performance indicator: 173 kWh/m2/yr\r\nApply: Keane Auctioneers (053) 9123072"
